github_url: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/issues/57"
body: "Observed on open [PR56](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/56), head `8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0`, rechecked current on 2026-11-03 at 20:05 UTC. The PR upgrades development SDK 10.28 →10.30 without changing repair implementation or tests.\n\n## Hosted evidence\n[Node 22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41706993031/job/126164822295) and [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41706993031/job/126164823666) each report 189 tests, 187 passed, 2 failed:\n- [repair-model.test.ts 58](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/test/repair-model.test.ts#L58): sequence 0 fails deep equality after JSON round-trip because the SDK receipt contains optional `undefined` author_source/source_kind/note properties that JSON omits.\n- [repairs.test.ts 49](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/test/repairs.test.ts#L49): repeating an unchanged revision-bound preview fails equality because `validation.records[].after.metadata.updated_at` differs between fresh staged validations.\n\n## Cause and goal\n[buildRepairPreview](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/src/repairs.ts#L177) forwards the entire `previewItemMutations` validation result into its public receipt. The host's [staged-record API addition](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1598) means that result now includes normalized staged records, not just the earlier validation summary.\n\nThe closed [authoring-repair feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/8805e866f7a55e1ac48f8b7ab9ab7979fca593e0/.agents/pm/features/pm-lint-authoring-repair-previews.toon) records SDK/JSON/TOON replay and 500-sequence evidence. The tests explicitly require serializable round-trip equality and unchanged-revision receipt equality. Actual newly forwarded optional properties and staged timestamps violate those existing comparisons. Stable plan identity and a fresh validation payload need an explicit compatibility contract rather than silently treating the candidate as certified.\n\n## Independent bounded check\nExecuted the exact current `buildRepairPreview` body under Node 24.22.1 with wholly synthetic SDK dependencies and two synthetic staged validation results. Revision, plan_key and repair patch stayed identical, while the different staged timestamp and optional undefined field were forwarded unchanged. This isolates the forwarding behavior; it is not a real SDK integration rerun. The hosted Node 22/26 jobs provide the real dependency evidence.\n\n## Acceptance and limits\nDefine which receipt fields are stable replay identity and which are freshly staged validation evidence, preserving the host's native semantics. Ensure SDK/JSON/TOON consumers have an explicit comparable representation for optional fields, and update implementation/tests consistently with that documented contract. Keep stale-revision refusal, zero source-byte changes, independent SDK readback, native metadata preservation and all 500 sequences at unchanged coverage thresholds. Rerun Node 22/26 and packed acceptance on the final head.\n\nThis report does not establish source tracker mutation, an invalid mechanical patch or a core staged-record defect. It establishes two current upgrade acceptance failures and their receipt-shape cause. All 56 all-status GitHub issues/PRs, current PR56 discussion and all current canonical tracker records were checked. The closed repair feature supplies the goal; no existing record owns these SDK 10.30 compatibility failures. No installs, provider requests or external mutations were performed during the independent check.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-04T15:06:45Z)\n>\n> Fresh compatibility evidence, checked 2026-11-04 at 15:06 UTC: [PR #56](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/pull/56) is still at `875638bd94480e1322bbc2b5197324022831c5ef`, now pinning SDK `2026.11.1` rather than the earlier `2026.10.30`. The dependency-only PR does not repair these implementations or tests.\n> \n> [Node 22](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41838613179/job/126603972470) and [Node 26](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/actions/runs/41838613179/job/126603972158) each ran 189 tests: 186 passed, 3 failed. Both logs identify the tested checkout as GitHub's merge commit `2f93f2d619a66c1289d5e8f215c75fbe7a224ddb`, combining head `875638bd` with base `ad42b30d`; this is hosted merge-check evidence, not a local bare-head rerun.\n> \n> The two original failures persist:\n> - repair-model transport sequence 0 loses optional undefined fields during JSON round-trip.\n> - repeated mechanical preview differs in staged `after.metadata.updated_at`.\n> \n> There is also a third upgrade acceptance failure: [test/rules.test.ts:358](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/875638bd94480e1322bbc2b5197324022831c5ef/test/rules.test.ts#L337-L361) expects PML005 to flag the terminal fixture after claiming, closing, and aging only `updated_at`; it receives false rather than true. [staleWork](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/875638bd94480e1322bbc2b5197324022831c5ef/src/rules.ts) requires active work or retained ownership before evaluating recent activity. The log alone does not establish whether this is a stale fixture assumption under newer SDK close/claim semantics or a product defect; do not force closed work to retain a claim merely to satisfy the old assertion.\n> \n> The existing [repair feature contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/875638bd94480e1322bbc2b5197324022831c5ef/.agents/pm/features/pm-lint-authoring-repair-previews.toon) and [rule contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-lint/blob/875638bd94480e1322bbc2b5197324022831c5ef/.agents/pm/features/pm-lint-rules.toon) supply the goals. Expected: explicit serializable/replay receipt semantics and stale-claim coverage that follows current native SDK lifecycle behavior. Actual: the current upgrade remains blocked in coverage tests before the full release/packed acceptance sequence can complete.\n> \n> Acceptance addition: reconcile the closed-item fixture with the SDK's documented post-close ownership state, independently assert that state, preserve positive stale-live-claim and activity tests, and rerun the existing full Node 22/26 and packed gates at unchanged thresholds. Keep the original transport, zero-write, stale-revision and 500-sequence requirements.\n> \n> Deduplication: all 59 all-status GitHub issues/PRs and all 26 canonical tracker records at main `c26764b9` were inspected; the open imported record for this issue remains the existing owner. No duplicate issue created. No local SDK integration rerun, source mutation, dependency change, release or deployment is claimed.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-04T23:38:52Z)\n>\n> Fixed by #56 (merged as bd6846c): the pm-toolchain bump to pm-cli 2026.11.4 now clears typed fields with `unset` instead of placeholder sentinels (pm-cli GH-1614), its tests pass and its coverage meets the unchanged thresholds. The agent's commits were reviewed by a read-only codex reviewer before the merge."
